            <ArticleTitle>Hantavirus Pulmonary Syndrome Caused by Maripa Virus in French Guiana, 2008-2016.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1722-1725</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.170842</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report 5 human cases of hantavirus pulmonary syndrome found during surveillance in French Guiana in 2008-2016; of the 5 patients, 4 died. This pathogen should continue to be monitored in humans and rodents in effort to reduce the occurrence of these lethal infections in humans stemming from ecosystem disturbances.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
